s south gable falls behind its tall stack to a level coped wall head (#1248)\n\nBehind the tall stack, the 1888 plate's coping runs level at about 10.95 m back to the\nfront block's rear wall, into the flank's vanishing point (u 5.9 at 10.96 m, u -0.3 at\n10.98 m through the T-2541 camera), and the Chicagology print draws the same: a short\nsteep fall from the stack, then one level line past the second stack. Neither shows\nany roof over it. The build's coping instead fell down the 22.4-degree rear slope.\n\nK01's gable roof learns `rear_fall` (coped ends only): the rear slope falls from the\nridge at its pitch to a flat deck, and the coped parapet falls with it to a level wall\nhead, its coping's top at wall_head_m, its head running head_back_m behind the ridge.\n1811 takes 10.95 m, the street's 61.2 degrees and 0.1 m. Rendered, the coping stands\nwithin about 4 px of the plate from x 533 to 566 and the second stack's top at y 394\nagainst 393-396. Every other K01 house re-emits byte-identical (k01_emit --check);\nthe 31 meshes that read K01's generators are re-emitted for their manifest inputs.\n\nThe range behind the block steps down to about 8.6 m in both pictures, where the\nbuild carries it at 11.4 m: T-3077.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:26:16Z","author":{"name":"Kevin Haas","email":"kevinroberthaas@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","private":false,"owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k